  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Let the co-ordinates of one vertex of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the other two vertices lie on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8484;</mi></math>, if the area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sq</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>units</mi></math> and the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> has length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>21</mn></msqrt></math> units, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to _______.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>The co-ordinates of one vertex of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the other two vertices lie on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0137_cf0fff0a99a4.png\" style=\"width: 346px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>Now any point on the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now direction ratio of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>,</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Also given area,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>21</mn></msqrt><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>21</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>19</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now on solving equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
